<title>USA: Alcoa to buy Inespal SA aluminum businesses.</title>
<headline>Alcoa to buy Inespal SA aluminum businesses.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aluminum Co of America and the Spanish State Entity for Industrial Participations said Tuesday that Alcoa has signed a letter of intent to acquire the main sectors of the aluminum business of Inespal SA for an undisclosed price.</p>
<p>The sale, which is expected to close before the end of the year, includes an alumina refinery, three aluminum smelters, aluminum rolling, foil and extrusion businesses, and related facilities.</p>
<p>Inispal is an integrated aluminum producer with revenues of $1.1. billion in 1996.</p>
</text>
